			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1734596">
									

<p>The use of &quot;memetic&quot; here is really nagging at me. Especially this bit:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Notably, a small segment of the population seems to be particularly vulnerable to SCP-1345-B's memetic effect, taking efforts to learn more about it and spread the knowledge to others, despite evidence that SCP-1345 never happened.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is&#8230; normal. Humans do this by themselves, so I have a hard time swallowing that it's all because of a mind-control machine. Also, what would make this memetic is if the affected subjects are capable of spreading the effect to others; all we have here is that the machine made the initial subjects believe; all subsequent believers are, well, just conspiracy nuts.</p>
<p>Unless you can convince me that this is actually memetic propagation at work, I'm not going to tag it as such.</p>

